course: dictionary
lesson: 12458
title: Deferential
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Deferential means showing great respect and politeness to someone, often by agreeing with them or letting them decide. Look at the clues in the sentence: who is being respected, and how do they behave? «She gave a deferential bow to the queen.» A bow is a sign of respect, so deferential means respectful.
explain: Being deferential to teachers and elders is polite. But «He was so deferential that he never told the teacher she had made a mistake.» The clue is never told: being too deferential can stop people speaking up when something is wrong.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «She gave a respectful bow to the queen» still makes sense, so deferential is a good match. Deferential is an adjective, and we can compare it: «The butler was more deferential than the cook.»
fact: Deferential is an adjective. Its comparative form is more deferential.
fact: «Deferential» means showing great respect and politeness, often by agreeing with someone or letting them decide.
fact: In history, servants, courtiers and citizens were often deferential to kings and lords: they bowed, curtsied and spoke politely.
fact: Being deferential is often good manners, but being too deferential can mean you never speak up when something is wrong.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «deferential to», «deferential tone» and «overly deferential».
exercise: «The young servant gave a deferential bow to the lord.» What does deferential mean here? | Showing anger and rudeness | Running away fast | Laughing loudly | *Showing respect and politeness
exercise: «He was deferential to his teacher and always waited for her to speak first.» Find and copy the word that shows he respected her. | waited | *deferential | always | teacher
exercise: Lily says, «Her deferential tone made everyone feel important.» What kind of tone is a deferential tone? | A tone that is hard to hear | *A polite, respectful tone | A loud, angry tone | A tone that is always joking
test: «The dog sat by the door, deferential and still, waiting for its owner.» What does deferential suggest? | *Respectful and patient | Angry and hungry | Bored and sleepy | Wild and noisy
test: Mia's friend says, «Don't be so deferential, tell him he's wrong!» What does the friend mean? | You should bow lower to him | You should agree with everything he says | You should leave the room | *You should stop being so respectful and speak up
exam: Which sentence uses deferential correctly? | «The rain was deferential and fell all day.» | «The football was deferential across the field.» | *«The clerk was deferential to the manager and waited for her decision.» | «She was deferential to the loud music.»
